Wave 2 of the ratchet. Read /home/joshu/.lares-scratch/crud/common.md again (the ruling, the crud and live-law lines, the apertures, the burn classes).

Your own wave-1 handback: /home/joshu/.lares-scratch/crud/sol-b/out.md. Your twin's: /home/joshu/.lares-scratch/crud/sol-a/out.md. Your twin swept other ground with the same brief.

Do these four things, read-only (repo untouched, no suites):
# ''VERIFY your twin's findings.'' Open every cited file:line. Mark each CONFIRMED, WRONG (cite what the code really does) or LIVE-LAW (it guards foreign, forged or malformed input, or a shape the code must never take, so keep it). Pay most care to B1/B2/B3 claims; a wrong burn deletes load-bearing wood.
# ''RE-CHECK your own findings'' with the same eye, and drop any you now doubt.
# ''RATCHET.'' At each aperture your twin covered thinly, hunt once more for what both of you missed, especially unworded crud: a second branch in a reader, `?? oldField`, an exists-check on a retired path, a test that pins an old name, a census whose only rows name retired shapes.
# ''For each B-class finding, name its burn unit:'' the files that must change together in one commit (the check, its error kind, its tests, its census rows, its canon line) so a builder can burn it whole.

Write the handback to /home/joshu/.lares-scratch/crud/sol-b/out2.md (never final.md). Sections:
(a) your twin's findings with your verdict;
(b) your own, kept or dropped;
(c) new finds;
(d) burn units, grouped and ordered so each unit builds alone. Mark [wave-d] units that sit on origin/feature/green-jello-dinosaur-5&#45;-k15-wave-d, and separate units on the span from units on that branch;
(e) the witness rule that would keep the crud from regrowing. Name the instrument it extends (e.g. tools/evergreen-boundary.mjs) and the exact pattern.

Plain short sentences; every claim cites file:line.

